        <headline>yellow warning - snowfall - in effect</headline>
        <description>
Snowfall, with localized amounts near 15 cm, will begin this morning and end this evening. 

Snow levels will be around 1600 m with the heaviest snow falling over higher elevations, including the Columbia Icefield area.

###

Travel will likely be challenging. Visibility will likely be reduced at times.

Please continue to monitor alerts and forecasts issued by Environment Canada. To report severe weather, send an email to ABstorm@ec.gc.ca, call 1-800-239-0484 or post reports on social media using #ABStorm.
</description>
